---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import {release} from '../data/release';import {product} from '../data/site';
---
<Layout title="Download Floatlet for Windows"><section class="page wrap"><p class="eyebrow">A LITTLE SOMETHING FOR YOUR DESKTOP</p><h1>Meet your new<br/>little companion.</h1><p class="lead">Free, open-source software for Windows 10 and 11.</p>{release?<div class="release-panel"><span class="eyebrow">{release.channel.toUpperCase()} RELEASE · {release.version}</span><h2>Floatlet for Windows</h2><dl class="release-meta"><div><dt>Architecture</dt><dd>x64 · Intel & AMD</dd></div><div><dt>Requirements</dt><dd>{release.windows}</dd></div><div><dt>Download size</dt><dd>{(release.size/1024).toFixed(1)} KiB · EXE</dd></div><div><dt>Published</dt><dd>{release.date}</dd></div></dl><a class="button" href={release.url} data-event="download_click" data-placement="download">Download Floatlet.exe ↓</a><p class="fine">Unsigned release. No ARM64 package is available. Snapdragon PCs run this x64 build through Windows emulation.</p><h3 style="font-size:18px;letter-spacing:0;margin-top:24px">SHA-256</h3><code class="checksum">{release.sha256}</code><a href={release.notes}>Release notes ↗</a><p><a href={release.zipUrl}>ZIP with installation scripts</a></p><p class="fine">The EXE runs directly. For a managed per-user install, use the ZIP and its install script.</p></div>:<div class="status-notice">The renamed release is being verified. <a href={product.repository+'/releases'}>View available GitHub releases</a>.</div>}<div class="prose"><h2>Before you install</h2><p>This is an early, unsigned preview. Windows may show a publisher or reputation warning. Verify the source and checksum before deciding whether to run it. Do not disable Windows security protections.</p><p><a href="/docs/install/" data-event="install_guide_open" data-placement="download">Installation guide</a> · <a href="/docs/uninstall/">Uninstall and local data</a> · <a href="/changelog/">Changelog</a></p><h2>A few useful answers</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Does Floatlet need an account?</summary><p>No account is required for the app. A Google Calendar subscription is optional.</p></details><details><summary>Will it work on my Snapdragon PC?</summary><p>The x64 build runs through Windows emulation. Native ARM64 delivery remains unavailable.</p></details><details><summary>Does the tray move my files?</summary><p>No. It stores references to originals. Outgoing drag uses copy semantics. Removing a tray entry does not delete the original.</p></details><details><summary>How much memory does it use?</summary><p>Two short 0.3.0 observations ranged from about 47 to 124 MiB private memory and 0.20% to 0.57% total-machine CPU. Activity was uncontrolled. These are not current-release benchmarks or battery measurements.</p></details><details><summary>Can I contribute?</summary><p>Yes. Floatlet is MIT licensed. Contributions to the main repository require the owner's review and passing checks.</p></details></div></div></section></Layout>
